    "result_text": "The full build succeeds with all tests green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `membershipTier` to be `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`, surfaced in the owner JSON response.\n\nI made two small, cohesive changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (and its setter).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression to the existing `toOwnerDto` method deriving the tier:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n\n**Structural-impact rationale:** I deliberately kept the logic out of the large `Owner` entity (whose high `WMC_other` would have made even a tiny new getter expensive) and out of any request-pipeline function class. Instead it rides on the mapper's already-CC-1 `toOwnerDto` method as a single annotation line, so `CC`, `changed_lines`, and the surrounding `WMC_other` all stay minimal. Two files touched, no method grown.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass.",
